.TH Yahtzee 6l.SH NAMEyahtzee \- the game of yahtzee.SH SYNOPSIS.B yahtzee.B [\-d] [\-N] [\-s] [\-h].SH DESCRIPTION.I Yahtzeeis a computer simulation of the game of the same name.This version of Yahtzee allows up to six players, whereplayers can be either users at the same terminalor a computer simulation of a player..PPFull on\-line help is available at all times by pressingthe question mark character. If you are unfamiliar withthe rules a rule book is also available at all timesby pressing the 'b' key..PPOptions are:.TP.B  \-ddon't use the standout mode of the terminal.TP.B  \-Nplay.I yahtzeenon-stop, good if all players are computer simulations.TP.B  \-sdisplay the high score file.TP.B  \-hgive command line options.PPAt the end of each game the player with the highest scoreis eligible to have their score recorded in the highscore file..SH BUGSUnknown, but please send bug problems to {utzoo,utcsri,lsuc}!hcr!stacey..SH AUTHORStacey Campbell \- HCR Corporation, Toronto, Canada, 1988.